=== Introduction
--- Psalms 18–20 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalms 18–20
sub: The Lord is my rock • The heavens declare the glory of God • We will remember the name of the LORD
refs: Psalm 18:2; Psalm 19:1; Psalm 20:7
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse. Press C for the whole chapter.

=== Psalm 18
--- Psalm 18 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 18
sub: My rock, my fortress, and my deliverer
refs: Psalm 18:1

--- I will love thee, O Lord
kicker: Psalm 18 · My strength
big: Psalm 18:1
p: **Psalm 18** is one of the first long-form songs of David, and it reflects his own experience with the Lord, his trust in God, and deliverance from his enemies, while weaving together prophetic views of Jesus, the doctrines of salvation, the end times wrath and Kingdom of God.
p: Ultimately, the Psalm gives us understanding of Who the Lord is and why He is worthy of our trust, today.

--- My rock, my fortress
kicker: Psalm 18 · Who the Lord is
scripture: Psalm 18:2-3; Psalm 18:25-26 | mark: The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful
p: The Lord is our strength. Our rock. Our fortress. Our deliverer. Our strength. Trustworthy. Our buckler, the horn of our salvation, our high tower. He is worthy to be praised. He is merciful to those that are merciful. Upright in all His ways to those that walk in them. Pure to the pure and froward to the froward.

--- His way is perfect
kicker: Psalm 18 · The word of the Lord is tried
big: Psalm 18:30 | mark: his way is perfect: the word of the LORD is tried
p: His way is perfect, His word is tried and trusted, and the strength and shield of those that place that trust in Him.

--- Who is a rock save our God?
kicker: Psalm 18 · No other rock
big: Psalm 18:31
p: There is no other rock than the Lord. There is no other name given but Jesus. He is the fulfillment of the word, the word made flesh, the promise of God come down from Heaven. The Christ. And He liveth.

--- The shield of thy salvation
kicker: Psalm 18 · Thy right hand
big: Psalm 18:35 | mark: thy gentleness hath made me great
p: The shield of salvation is given, by the right-hand of God. His gentleness has made those who trust Him great.

--- The Lord liveth
kicker: Psalm 18 · My rock
big: Psalm 18:46

--- The head of the heathen
kicker: Psalm 18 · A people I have not known
scripture: Psalm 18:43-44 | mark: a people whom I have not known shall serve me
p: The Lord is praised among the heathen. The strangers hear and obey. The people who were not a people are come, and are subdued under the throne of David, to his Seed. To His anointed, evermore.

--- Hail stones and coals of fire
kicker: Psalm 18 · The enemies destroyed
scripture: Psalm 18:13-14; Psalm 18:41 | mark: hail stones and coals of fire; They cried, but there was none to save them
p: The enemies of David, like the enemies of Christ, are crushed before them by the fiery and fierce judgment of God. Rains of fire and brimstone, hail and lightnings, leading the wicked to cry out, and hide themselves from His fury. And ultimately be destroyed by His coming.

--- According to my righteousness
kicker: Psalm 18 · A rewarder
scripture: Psalm 18:20; Psalm 18:24 | mark: according to the cleanness of my hands
p: The Lord then is a rewarder of those that trust in Him, who diligently seek Him. Who follow His ways and obey His statutes. He will reward us for the righteousness we have shown, and the recompense for our cleanliness in His sight. The righteousness of Christ imputed on His children. The gold, silver and precious stones we build upon that foundation.

--- Thou wilt light my candle
kicker: Psalm 18 · He lifts us up
scripture: Psalm 18:28-29 | mark: thou wilt light my candle
p: He lifts us up, strengthening us to do great deeds in His name. He fills us with His light.

--- He heard my voice
kicker: Psalm 18 · In my distress
scripture: Psalm 18:6-8 | mark: he heard my voice out of his temple
p: He hears our cries. He comes to our aid. He destroys the wicked for our sake, in the anger kindled by their sin against Him and their treatment of His children.

--- Among the heathen
kicker: Psalm 18 · Thanks
big: Psalm 18:49
center: Amen

--- The complete picture
kicker: Psalm 18 · Songs of deliverance
big: Psalm 18:50 | mark: Great deliverance giveth he to his king
p: Songs of deliverance and praise, with the appearance of the Lord as a consuming fire, yet displaying tender mercies to His beloved, those that place their trust in Him, and who call upon the Lord, are found throughout the book of Psalms.
p: The reassurance to believers that what God has done for David will be done for us, His name and word are worthy, and are to be trusted. The picture of salvation and judgment. All are detailed repeatedly, just as much as songs of despair and pleas for God's intervention. But both styles of song contain thanksgiving and praise for His grace and mercy, and all the blessings He has already provided those that love Him.
p: Taken as a whole, Psalms gives us the complete picture of the Christian life. They give us a model of prayer and praise that fits every stage of our growth and development, while also dripping with doctrine, teaching us the truth of God.

=== Psalm 19
--- Psalm 19 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 19
sub: The heavens declare • The law of the LORD is perfect
refs: Psalm 19:1

--- Without excuse
kicker: Psalm 19 · The testimony of creation
p: **Psalm 19** is fairly short, yet packed with doctrine, teaching the purpose of creation, the testimony of God to all creatures, the picture of Christ, and the establishment of the law of the Lord in nature itself, that there is no excuse, while the believer is given constant reminders of His judgements.
scripture: Romans 1:18-20 | mark: so that they are without excuse

--- The heavens declare the glory of God
kicker: Psalm 19 · Day unto day
scripture: Psalm 19:1-2 | mark: The heavens declare the glory of God
p: The heavens declare the glory of God. Looking upon the night sky we see His precision and power. And as the day follows day and night follows night, each with the passing of the sun and the stars, we are given evidence of His might.

--- No speech nor language
kicker: Psalm 19 · Their line is gone out
scripture: Psalm 19:3-4 | mark: There is no speech nor language, where their voice is not heard
p: The things of creation speak without words, that all man may understand. They don't need a language. They don't need to be explained. Man sees the passage of time, seasons, years, decades even, in heavenly bodies.
p: The vain hypothetical of a savage on a remote island, never hearing the gospel, is undone by the understanding that all nature is a parable and a testament of God, showing men truth.

--- As a bridegroom
kicker: Psalm 19 · The sun
scripture: Psalm 19:5-6 | mark: as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber
p: The boldness of the sun breaking forth in the morning is as the risen Christ, returning in glory, a picture of the Creator Who is blessed forever, amen.
p: Nature teaches us God's law. His ways.
big: 1 Corinthians 11:14 | mark: Doth not even nature itself teach you

--- Written in their hearts
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 19:1–6
p: His wrath is revealed against those who sin, even without the oracles of God documenting His commandments. The Spirit showing mankind the results of their transgressions. The understanding that murder, adultery, lying, stealing, all of these things that do harm to your neighbor and are a shame before God, are known.
scripture: Romans 2:11-16 | mark: Which shew the work of the law written in their hearts

--- The oracles of God
kicker: Cross references • Psalm 19:7
p: Man can see the law of God, know it written in their hearts, watch the outcome of their behavior and the wrath upon those who sin, and know they are guilty before the consuming fire which is God.
p: How much more are we who have His statutes and commandments by the oracles of God?
scripture: Romans 3:1-2 | mark: unto them were committed the oracles of God
p: The advantage given Israel, and held by the Jews in Paul's day, is now given to the world. That everyone may know His word.

--- The law of the Lord is perfect
kicker: Psalm 19 · Converting the soul
big: Psalm 19:7 | mark: The law of the LORD is perfect, converting the soul
p: If the day declares His righteousness and the night His knowledge, and the very nature of things speaks to His wrath, then the oracles of God give us the hope of His mercy. God is a rewarder to those that diligently seek Him.

--- The fear of the Lord is clean
kicker: Psalm 19 · The statutes of the Lord
scripture: Psalm 19:8-9 | mark: The fear of the LORD is clean
p: The fear of the Lord is clean, and known to all men. The fool may say in their heart there is no God, but the wise fear Him, even if they don't know scripture.

--- Sweeter than honey
kicker: Psalm 19 · Great reward
scripture: Psalm 19:10-11 | mark: More to be desired are they than gold; sweeter also than honey
p: The truth is more desirable than gold, sweeter than honey. Its pursuit is its own reward, spurring us to seek Him. The warnings and rewards, motivation to learn His ways.
p: And, in that knowledge, we find His word, and from that word, salvation.

--- Cleanse thou me
kicker: Psalm 19 · Presumptuous sins
scripture: Psalm 19:12-13 | mark: cleanse thou me from secret faults; Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous sins
p: In Him we are cleansed from our iniquity. In Him we are conformed to His image, kept back from presumptuous sin. Made upright. His righteousness imputed on us that we may be transformed. To be our strength and the Lord our Redeemer.

--- All creation is a parable
kicker: Application • Creation
p: We are blessed to have the knowledge of the truth before us. His inspired and preserved word, that we may know Him. And God does not leave those without the oracles lacking.
p: But for the children of God, creation gives us reassurance and opportunities to worship Him for His might and glory. To have reminders that He loves us.
p: To every seed we sow that comes to fruition. To every shooting star, or bird in flight, or wave crashing on the shore, we are able to look at the Lord in awe. Babies born to the death of the elderly, spring following winter, the setting sun and darkest night...all creation is a parable to those with ears to hear and eyes to see.

--- New creatures in Christ
kicker: Application • Creation
p: To know God loves us. And His mercy upon us is evidence to others seeking truth. The light in us shines that others may see and glorify God.
p: We are to be as the firmament, as the rising sun and the crashing wave. His children are meant to teach the heathen who seeks the Lord, as much as anything in creation. Because we are new creatures in Christ, brought forth as a testimony to God's greatness.

--- My strength, and my redeemer
kicker: Psalm 19 · The words of my mouth
big: Psalm 19:14
center: Amen

=== Psalm 20
--- Psalm 20 [title]
overline: The Book of Psalms
heading: Psalm 20
sub: The name of the LORD our God
refs: Psalm 20:1

--- The name of the God of Jacob
kicker: Psalm 20 · Out of Zion
scripture: Psalm 20:1-3 | mark: the name of the God of Jacob defend thee; strengthen thee out of Zion; accept thy burnt sacrifice
p: **Psalm 20** is yet another song of praise and worship for the salvation that is in Christ Jesus.
p: The name of the God of Jacob. The Lord that strengthens us out of Zion. The one offering forever, the burnt sacrifice. Christ Jesus.

--- Fulfil all thy counsel
kicker: Psalm 20 · Thy counsel
big: Psalm 20:4
p: The love of God has been granted to us in his grace, and his counsel is wisdom; trust in the Lord.

--- We will set up our banners
kicker: Psalm 20 · In the name of our God
big: Psalm 20:5 | mark: in the name of our God we will set up our banners
p: We will rejoice in the salvation given to us in the name of our God. We will set up banners in His holy name. He is Christ Jesus, and God hears all our petitions, lifted up in His name.

--- The Lord saveth his anointed
kicker: Psalm 20 · His right hand
big: Psalm 20:6 | mark: the LORD saveth his anointed
p: The Lord saves His anointed. He did not leave his soul to see corruption. His anointed was not left in hell. The saving strength of His right hand. Christ Jesus.

--- Some trust in chariots
kicker: Psalm 20 · We will remember the name
scripture: Psalm 20:7-8 | mark: we will remember the name of the LORD our God; we are risen, and stand upright
p: Some trust in the power of this world, their own strength, their own works. And they will be brought down low. He will say depart from me. I never knew you.
p: But to those of us who trust in the name of the Lord, our God, we are risen and made to stand upright. In Christ Jesus.

--- Save, Lord
kicker: Psalm 20 · Save, Lord
big: Psalm 20:9 | mark: Save, LORD
p: Save, Lord. In the name of the King of Kings and the Lord of lords, Christ Jesus.

--- Horses and chariots
kicker: Psalm 20 · Some trust in chariots
big: Psalm 20:7
p: This verse is often quoted, and has inspired generations of believers. But in practice it can be difficult. We often seek reassurance from our material, wealth and position.
p: David, writing this Psalm with dual purpose (at least), the prophetic imagery of Christ Jesus and the surety of his salvation, but also as an intercessional prayer before a battle against a well-armed and equipped foe.

--- We have already overcome
kicker: Application • Trust
p: David's showing us that it is better to trust in the Lord than all the horses and chariots in the world. That in our battles, even if we are seemingly overmatched by our enemy, we are still victorious in God.
p: What a comfort. What a blessing. That we can stand fast, and be sure of our deliverance. That we can trust in the Lord in all things, because we've first trusted in Him, our eternal security.
p: When we are weak we are made strong. God uses us to confound the wise. We have already overcome in Christ. And we should rejoice in our salvation.

